## D1 — record only, one join, not a pass gate
Viewer-side burst of 1.5 s from the first packet, same advertised address via lossy.py, fractional loss 0.
Chromium join: connectMs 1578, firstPresentedMs 1777, picture 1280x720, audioPeakHz 439 (quieter: peakDb -75, rms 0.0184).
Proxy: to_edge 46, to_edge_dropped 25, to_client 191, to_client_dropped 0.
1.2 s is not a pass gate. One phase only.

## D2 — publisher media was actually dropped; loss-cause does not exist on this pin
WHIP from Chromium, fake capture of an 8 s 1280x720 testsrc2 y4m plus 440 Hz.
Sender degradationPreference maintain-resolution, maxBitrate 2500000. Without that, Chromium encoded 640x360 under bandwidth pressure. That 640x360 attempt is discarded.
A burst from the first packet only dropped 25 ICE packets and missed the media. Discarded.
Recorded run: lossy.py --burst-after 3 --burst 1.5, fractional loss 0.
Encoded size at t=3,6,9 s: 1280x720. keyFramesEncoded stayed 1. pliCount stayed 0. nackCount went 0 then 4.
Proxy: to_edge 2793, to_edge_dropped 396, to_client 220, to_client_dropped 9.
Decoded d2.ivf: vp8 1280x720, 181 frames, 6.03 s, about 2095 kb/s. frames/d2.png is 1280x720, counter box 366 bright pixels.
Raw media timestamps have a 833 ms gap (2981144 µs to 3814144 µs) during the burst, plus a 134 ms gap earlier.
rg of the edge log for loss-cause or cause=loss: 0. The unpatched pin has no loss-cause tag. No second keyframe was produced.
D2's after gate (loss-cause PLI and a post-burst keyframe ≤ 1.2 s) is not met, and cannot be met before the patch.

## F — policy off, probe boundary
8 s raw of the ffmpeg 1280x720 VP8 publisher (1500k, gop 30).
groups=3 frames=62 key_bytes=71624 other_bytes=323167 share=0.1814 quality=missing.
ffprobe f.ivf: vp8 1280x720, 62 frames, duration 2.07 s, about 1530 kb/s.
No ingest hook exists on this pin, so this is the policy-off cost, not the saturated-hook row.

